<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36488" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξάγιστος</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξαγίζω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>devoted to evil, accursed, abominable,</i> usu.
			of persons, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				25.93
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				6.89
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.265
			</span></i>, etc.; of things, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιμήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aeschin.
					3.113
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βουλεύματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Jul.
					<u>Or.</u>
					2.99b
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				1526
			</span></i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἃ δ᾽ ἐξάγιστα μηδὲ κινεῖται
			λόγῳ</span> what things are <i>matters of religion</i>: cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
